 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Not given in the sources. The light-space rasterization adds an additional pass over the Gaussians [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources. Requires additional buffer for `record_front_tau` aligned with the Gaussian buffer [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Provides accurate self-shadowing effects in volume rendering. Compatible with existing training pipelines [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Requires additional computation for the light pass. Fallback mode may be less efficient or accurate than rasterization [S1, unofficial].
-- **When to Use:** When self-shadowing effects are desired in 3D Gaussian Splatting scenes [S1, unofficial].
-- **When Not to Use:** When performance is critical and self-shadowing is not necessary [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ for $N$ Gaussians, plus sorting overhead $O(N \log N)$ per light pass.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for storing $T_{light}$ per Gaussian.
+*   **Performance:** Depends on the number of Gaussians and the resolution of the sun camera's rasterization pass.
+*   **Strengths:** Accurately models self-shadowing in volume rendering.
+*   **Limitations:** Requires an additional rasterization pass. Parallax error must be managed by camera setup.
 
 ## Background
-Developed for volume cloud rendering to model self-shadowing effects in 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1, unofficial]. The method was introduced to address the lack of front occlusion modeling in standard splatting pipelines by introducing a dedicated light-space accumulation pass [S1, unofficial]. It is used in real-time volume cloud viewers and training frameworks that require physically plausible shadowing without modifying the primary camera's EWA projection [S1, unofficial].
+Originated in the context of 4D Gaussian Splatting for volume clouds, specifically for rendering realistic lighting and shadowing effects [S1, unofficial]. The method was developed to address the lack of self-shadowing in standard 3D Gaussian Splatting rendering pipelines.
 
